# WAN-harness runtime state. `hb-wan-it` defaults `--data-dir` to these (wan_it/mod.rs: `./hb-wan-it-data`
# for serve, `./hb-wan-it-probe-data` for every probe subcommand), so a WAN run materialises them in the
# repo root, and the e2e runbook adds ./e2e-serve and ./e2e-seed the same way. Each holds an
# identity/identity.json carrying `nsec`, `browse_key_hex` and `transport_secret_hex` — REAL secret
# material, in a PUBLIC repo, previously untracked-and-unignored. That is one `git add -A` from
# publishing a browse key unsealed, which is INV-2's exact failure shape; ignoring them is the fence.
# (Nothing leaked: no commit on any branch or tag has ever touched these paths.)
hb-wan-it-data/
hb-wan-it-probe-data/
e2e-serve/
e2e-seed/
